A||||6||Alex4mula||Idle, fuel & Murphy||||1||
Z||000000||Alex4mula||09-26-2001||02:11 PM||||My 3.4 has been having this idle problem since installed and many times it stumbled when stopping suddenly, specially after a long run. Well, recently it was worst and worst. So the idea came up to exchange the GM MAP sensor from my other Formula to see what happened. I did and the problem was solved. Bought a new AC Delco, put it in and now is very smooth, although it still has some little idle search. I checked that several times with the AutoXray and couldn’t see anything wrong and no code was set. I remember I changed that MAP sensor three years ago (+-12K miles) with a replacement (Non AC Delco) one. What a crap. Anyway that was solved and I was very happy but not for long. <BR>Then I went to put back in the other Formula its MAP and the module/coil that I have borrowed for the RFTH trip. In the mean time I checked the EGR vacuum lines trying to find the culprit of a daily code 32. Well, I found that both solenoid vacuum lines were like straws sucking in an empty glass. I replaced them and installed everything back. Fired up and car started so so, ran about 7 seconds then started stumbling and misfiring. I checked the fuel and was very empty, so I poured 2 gallons of fuel and tried again. Nada. Only cranking noise and nothing else. Well, I put my fuel pressure gage and 0 psi. I can hear the click of the relay but not the pump. I don’t think a fuel filter can clog so bad to provide 0 psi fuel pressure. So I guess my fuel pump is gone. What I hate most is that this happens when I was just fixing something else not related. At least it didn’t let me stranded in the street. Oh well…<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||ray b||09-26-2001||03:40 PM||||runing dry will fry the pump not every time but way tooo many times.<BR>local gm wanted 139.00 for the pump even with discount to 115 still high.<BR>check your gas gauge pointer likes to slip out of true should be dead on f when full to the max not over the f line eazy to fix just move it to line up with f when full, i like to glue it in place.<P>------------------<BR>Question wonder and be wierd||||reg||1
Z||000002||87GTZ34||09-26-2001||10:12 PM||||Alex, Sorry to hear that.  Let me know if you what to use my ramps or borrow your 18mm stuff back.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  How'd the run for the hills go?  I couldn't reply to your mail as your address bounced higher than the stratosphere. What's up with that?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Wolfhound||09-27-2001||07:46 AM||||Alex, Since this happened while working on something else, Check all related connections, something could have been just bumped and loosened. Connector to fuel pump, oil pressure sensor, relay connection, fuse etc.<BR>Coy||||reg||1
Z||000004||Alex4mula||09-27-2001||09:06 AM||||Wolf; yeah, I checked most of it. It was late and a little dark so I have to go back and re-check again to be sure.<P>Ron; Ramps would be nice but how do I backup the car without power??  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> The RFTH was awesome. I have couple (7) photos since my other camera didn't work there and there was no time to stop and buy a disposable. Wolfhound has very nice pictures in other post.<P>Update: I guess after the computer adapted to the new MAP sensor now the idle search is almost gone. Remember, never buy non AC Delco sosnors for your car.||||reg||1
Z||000005||falconhulk||09-27-2001||09:13 AM||||I assume that you still have the stock fiero fuel pump?  If so there is a wire in the engine compartment right near the left hinge for the decklid.  Its to the right of the fuel pump relay.  If you disconnect this wire, it is just one wire with a black connector in the middle, and apply battery voltage the pump should kick in.  This will tell you if it is good.  I think this is in the haynes manual with pictures.  ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Formula88||09-27-2001||09:13 AM||||"How to backup car without power 101"<P>Get a remote starter switch.<BR>Put car in reverse.<BR>With your foot off the clutch, press the starter switch.<BR>Your starter will now pull the car up onto the ramps.<P>Next weeks lesson: "How to start a car without gasoline..."  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||6
